**CWE-942 (Overly Permissive CORS)**: Reflecting arbitrary `Origin` with `Allow-Credentials: true` lets attacker sites read authenticated responses cross-origin. Match against an exact `frozenset` allowlist and include `Vary: Origin` so caches do not poison headers:
```python
ALLOWED_ORIGINS = frozenset({'https://app.aegis_defense.com'})

def build_cors_headers(request_origin: str | None) -> dict[str, str]:
    if request_origin in ALLOWED_ORIGINS:
        return {
            'Access-Control-Allow-Origin': request_origin,
            'Access-Control-Allow-Credentials': 'true',
            'Vary': 'Origin',
        }
    return {'Vary': 'Origin'}
```
